<section class="cottage" id="cottage">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cottage-header">
      <p class="section-label">The 1913 Cottage</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">The Booth Cottage</h2>
      <div class="divider"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="cottage-body">
      <div class="cottage-text">
        <p class="drop-cap">
          Before the Booth House was finished, another Wright building stood on the same land:
          a small, flat-roofed cottage designed in 1913 as temporary housing for Sherman and
          Elizabeth Booth while their permanent home was under construction nearby. This
          one-story structure of approximately 880 square feet — plain, horizontal, almost austere by Prairie
          standards — turns out to be one of the most architecturally significant small buildings
          Wright ever produced.
        </p>

        <p>
          The cottage's flat roof, banded windows, strong horizontal lines, and compact footprint
          anticipate the Usonian house by more than two decades. Wright would not formally introduce
          the Usonian concept until the 1930s — a family of modest, affordable, single-story homes
          designed for the American middle class, characterized by exactly the features visible here
          in 1913: the flat roof, the horizontal emphasis, the integration of the house with its
          landscape, the lack of attic or basement. Preservationists regard the cottage as a
          critical missing link in Wright's development, a proto-Usonian executed when the architect
          was still in his Prairie period.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="pull-quote">
          "Preservationists believe the cottage is worth saving because it anticipates the
          Usonian houses Wright designed from the 1930s to his death in 1959."
          <cite>— Chicago Magazine, 2019</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <p>
          After the Booth family vacated it, the cottage changed hands multiple times and was
          incorporated into later residential development on the original Booth estate. By 2019
          it had come under new ownership, and the new owners sought to demolish it. The Glencoe
          Historical Society, the Frank Lloyd Wright Building Conservancy, and Landmarks Illinois
          scrambled to organize a rescue. In 2019, Landmarks Illinois named the Booth Cottage
          one of the Most Endangered Historic Places in Illinois. The campaign raised more than
          $300,000 in private donations.
        </p>

        <h3 class="cottage-subhead">The Move</h3>

        <p>
          On July 21, 2020, the Glencoe Historical Society executed one of the more unusual
          preservation operations in Illinois history: a physical relocation of a Frank Lloyd
          Wright building. The original portion of the cottage was lifted from its foundation
          and moved to Park 7N — Ravine Bluffs Park — a short distance away, on land that had
          itself once been part of the Booth estate. The Glencoe Park District granted the
          Historical Society a 99-year land lease at $1 per year. The new site, at the foot
          of Ravine Bluffs, places the cottage within the original landscape of the development
          it was meant to serve.
        </p>

        <p>
          By May 2025, approximately 80% of exterior restoration work was complete. The
          Historical Society was fundraising an additional $350,000 to finish the interior
          restoration and open the building to the public as a museum, research center, and
          program space focused on Wright's work in Glencoe and the Prairie School.
        </p>

        <div class="cottage-specs">
          <div class="spec-item">
            <span class="spec-label">Designed</span>
            <span class="spec-value">1913</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-item">
            <span class="spec-label">Current Address</span>
            <span class="spec-value">Ravine Bluffs Park (Park 7N), Glencoe</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-item">
            <span class="spec-label">Size</span>
            <span class="spec-value">~880 sq ft, one story</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-item">
            <span class="spec-label">Steward</span>
            <span class="spec-value">Glencoe Historical Society</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="cottage-sidebar">
        <figure class="cottage-figure">
          <div class="cottage-img-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/ravine/cottage-exterior.jpg"
              alt="The Booth Cottage, Glencoe, Illinois — designed by Frank Lloyd Wright, 1913"
              loading="lazy"
              onerror="this.parentElement.classList.add('no-image')"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>The Booth Cottage — designed 1913, relocated 2020</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="cottage-fact-box">
          <h4 class="fact-box-title">Architectural Significance</h4>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Flat roof — unusual for Prairie period (1913)</li>
            <li>Banded horizontal windows</li>
            <li>No attic or basement</li>
            <li>Compact footprint integrated with landscape</li>
            <li>Proto-Usonian design, 20+ years before Wright's Usonian period</li>
            <li>One of 13 Wright structures associated with Glencoe</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cottage {
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .cottage-header {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-lg);
  }

  .cottage-body {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 300px;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .cottage-text p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .drop-cap::first-letter {
    font-size: 4.5rem;
    line-height: 0.8;
    float: left;
    margin-right: 0.1em;
    margin-top: 0.08em;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .pull-quote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .pull-quote cite {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-style: normal;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cottage-subhead {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .cottage-specs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .spec-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .spec-label {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .spec-value {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .cottage-sidebar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 7rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .cottage-figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cottage-img-frame {
    aspect-ratio: 4/3;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-border);
  }

  .cottage-img-frame.no-image {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .cottage-img-frame.no-image::after {
    content: "Photo coming soon";
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .cottage-img-frame.no-image img {
    display: none;
  }

  .cottage-img-frame img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .cottage-figure figcaption {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    font-style: italic;
  }

